{"base":"14d78b1419d2db8d3ff9427375548812f1ae08a1","description":"feat: store metadata values as JSON\n\n- Artifact.metadata is BTreeMap<String, serde_json::Value>\n- SetMetadata action carries a serde_json::Value\n- pretty display renders strings unquoted, other JSON shapes compact\n- CLI keeps wrapping its <VALUE> string for now; --json flag follows\n\nWhy: opaque strings forced every consumer to invent its own escaping\nfor structured annotations (SBOM blobs, build metadata). JSON values\nlet the data layer carry shape without forcing a parsing convention.\n\n\nfeat(cli): add --json flag to metadata set\n\n- default behaviour wraps <VALUE> in Value::String (unchanged UX)\n- --json parses <VALUE> as JSON (number, bool, null, array, object,\n  or quoted string)\n- new error::Metadata::InvalidJson reports parse failures inline\n\nWhy: now that the COB stores JSON values, the CLI needs an opt-in\nway to write structured annotations (SBOM blobs, build flags) without\nforcing every value through string escaping.","oid":"91d6a917526148e166ca248604479d3ad2f60796","type":"revision"}